Ollama v0.35.1 (commit b0c1ca4f): marshal a tool function without parameters
as an empty object schema.

WHY
---
Any OpenAI-compatible client that declares a function with no arguments gets
HTTP 400 from Ollama, for every request in the session:

    Unable to generate parser for this template. Automatic parser generation
    failed: JSON schema error at #: properties must be an object

Qwen Code 0.24.7 hits this on its first request: its get_goal and list_agents
tools have no "parameters" key, which the OpenAI API allows (leaving it out
means the function takes no arguments). The bug is not specific to gfx803 or
to any backend.

Ollama decodes each tool into api.ToolFunction and encodes it again for
llama-server. A missing "parameters" (or {} or {"type": "object"}) leaves
ToolFunctionParameters at its zero value, whose Properties pointer is nil and
whose Type is empty, so the request llama-server receives says
"parameters": {"type": "", "properties": null}. llama.cpp's JSON schema
builder rejects a non-object "properties". The same tools sent straight to
llama-server succeed, because llama.cpp itself normalizes a missing or empty
"parameters" to {"type": "object", "properties": {}}
(common_chat_tool_parameters).

To reproduce, with any model loaded:

    curl -s 127.0.0.1:11434/v1/chat/completions -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d \
      '{"model":"<model>","max_tokens":1,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":"hi"}],
        "tools":[{"type":"function","function":{"name":"t","description":"d"}}]}'

Without the patch this returns the error above; with it, a completion. Adding
"parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {}} works either way.

WHAT
----
ToolFunctionParameters gets a MarshalJSON that fills in Type "object" when it
is empty and an empty properties map when Properties is nil, so every encoder
of a tool (the llama-server request, the chat template's tool list) writes a
valid schema. The expectation in TestChatDebugRenderOnly, which recorded the
old "properties": null output, changes to match. go test ./api/ ./openai/
./server/ passes.

diff --git a/api/types.go b/api/types.go
index f5b04b14..a5182f7a 100644
--- a/api/types.go
+++ b/api/types.go
@@ -477,6 +477,22 @@ type ToolFunctionParameters struct {
 	Properties *ToolPropertiesMap `json:"properties"`
 }
 
+// MarshalJSON writes a function that takes no arguments as an object schema
+// with no properties. The OpenAI API lets a client leave out a function's
+// parameters, and the zero value would marshal to "type": "" and
+// "properties": null, which llama.cpp's tool-call parser generator rejects.
+func (t ToolFunctionParameters) MarshalJSON() ([]byte, error) {
+	type params ToolFunctionParameters
+	p := params(t)
+	if p.Type == "" {
+		p.Type = "object"
+	}
+	if p.Properties == nil {
+		p.Properties = NewToolPropertiesMap()
+	}
+	return json.Marshal(p)
+}
+
 func (t *ToolFunctionParameters) String() string {
 	bts, _ := json.Marshal(t)
 	return string(bts)
